---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Privacy Policy" description="Learn what information Easy Home Workout stores in your browser and how third-party media providers may receive basic connection data.">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">Your information</span><h1>Privacy policy</h1><p>Last updated November 10, 2026. This policy explains how Easy Home Workout handles information when you use this static website.</p></div></section>
  <section class="content-section"><div class="wrap" style="max-width:850px">
    <article class="panel"><h2>Information you enter</h2><p>This website does not ask you to create an account and has no backend or database that receives your workout activity. Workout history, challenge completion, and water-tracker entries are saved in your browser's local storage on the device you use. The site uses the browser storage keys <code>fhw-workouts</code>, <code>fhw-challenge</code>, and <code>fhw-water</code> for those features.</p><p>That information remains available to the website in the same browser until you clear it using the website controls or your browser settings. If you use browser sync, shared devices, extensions, or other software, those services may handle browser data under their own terms. Do not use a shared device if you do not want others with access to it to see locally saved progress.</p></article>
    <article class="panel"><h2>Third-party services and analytics</h2><p>Some pages load photographs from Unsplash and fonts from Google Fonts. The site also loads a Google Tag Manager container (GTM-PC24PD2H). The tags configured in that container may collect or send usage information to Google or other providers. The exact data and cookies involved depend on the tags enabled in the container. When your browser requests third-party resources, those providers may receive technical information such as your IP address, browser, and the requested resource. These services are subject to their providers' privacy policies and practices.</p><p>You can manage or block cookies and third-party requests through your browser settings. Blocking them may affect analytics and some site resources.</p></article>
    <article class="panel"><h2>Children and sensitive information</h2><p>This website is general fitness education and is not designed to collect personal information. Do not enter sensitive personal or health information into any browser feature or message you prepare from this site.</p></article>
    <article class="panel"><h2>Your choices</h2><p>You can clear saved workout, challenge, and water progress using the reset controls where available, or clear this site's local storage through your browser. Blocking third-party resources in your browser may prevent some fonts or photographs from loading.</p></article>
    <article class="panel"><h2>Policy updates</h2><p>This policy may be updated when the website's features or practices change. The date at the top indicates when this page was last revised.</p></article>
  </div></section>
</Layout>
